mutant: m072_sync_state_newest_pending_only
target: internal/ingest/syncstate/store.go
failure-mode: |
  Promotion only considers a DID's newest pending state, as the one-slot
  store did before specs/oracle/2026-09-26-disagg-pipelined-chain-state-hidden.md.
  When the verifier has already saved state for a later event, the earlier
  event's promotion makes nothing durable, so a batch commits its rows and a
  cursor past it with the DID's state behind. After a crash the successor
  resyncs needlessly or archives the event twice.
expected-detection: |
  TestStateStore_PipelinedSavesPromoteEach promotes the older of two pending
  revs and requires it durable. The layer 3 lifecycle oracle found the bug
  in about 4% of full and short runs, which is too rare for eight seeds to
  kill reliably, so the unit test is the executioner.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

